{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>Saying: to your seed I will give it.</b> The verse's saying ״לֵאמֹר״ — because He had not said to the three of them this formulation of ״לְזַרְעֲךָ אֶתְּנֶנָּה,״ therefore it says ״לֵאמֹר,״ meaning that the intent of the statement is this: ״לְזַרְעֲךָ אֶתְּנֶנָּה.״ And our Sages of blessed memory (Berakhot 18b) interpreted that He commanded him to go and say it to the fathers, etc., end of quote. And perhaps, since HaShem wanted Moses to say these things to them, it was in order to secure for him the fathers' favor and kindness, for that he toiled and labored on their behalf until bringing them to the place." "<b>And there you shall not pass.</b> Perhaps it intends to say to him that he will not need to pass there — to ascend by way of there, from the gate of heaven which is there — and our Sages of blessed memory said (Zohar vol. I 81a) that souls ascend only by way of there. And Moses, since he was gathered to the Shekhinah, behold his place is in the Holy, in the place that is there. And this is the meaning of the verse: ״וְשָׁמָּה לֹא״ — you will not need to pass to your place. And Scripture immediately follows by saying ״וַיָּמָת שָׁם״ וגו׳ ״עַל פִּי ה׳״ — understand:"], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 34, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:22:33.267292323Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}